course: dictionary
lesson: 3933
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Fry is one of them. It can be something you do in a pan, a kind of tiny fish, or a name. Context tells you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: «Her first dish is bubble-and-squeak (fried leftover cabbage and potato).» The words in brackets give the clue: fried means cooked in hot oil or fat. Fried is the past form of the verb fry, which is an action word.
explain: A capital letter can be a clue too. «Elizabeth Fry began visiting women prisoners in Newgate prison in London in 1813.» Here Fry is a person's surname, not a cooking word. Ask yourself: does this sentence make sense with a cooking meaning? If not, look for another meaning.
fact: Fry (verb) means to cook food in hot oil or fat in a pan.
fact: Fries means long thin pieces of potato cooked in oil; in the UK and Ireland they are called chips.
fact: Fry (noun) means very young fish just hatched from their eggs.
fact: «Small fry» means unimportant people, and «fry an egg» means cook an egg in a pan.
fact: British «chips» are American «fries»; British «crisps» are American «chips».
exercise: «Dad will fry two eggs for breakfast.» What does fry mean here? | To wash in cold water | *To cook in hot oil or fat in a pan | To buy from a shop | Throw away in the bin
exercise: In a science lesson the teacher says, «Fish lay eggs, and the fry hatch out.» What are the fry? | *Very young fish just hatched | Hot oil in a pan | Cooked chips | Small boats
exercise: «Elizabeth Fry visited prisoners in London in 1813.» In this sentence, what is Fry? | *A person's name | A cooking word | A plate of chips | A young fish
test:
«Her first dish is bubble-and-squeak (fried leftover cabbage and potato).» What does fried mean? | *Cooked in hot oil or fat | Chopped into small pieces | Boiled in water | Kept cold in a fridge
In the UK, what are «fries» called? | *Chips | Crisps | Sweets | Fish cakes
exam:
At a night market a child buys «a paper cone of fried crickets the way you might buy chips.» What does fried mean in «fried crickets»? | Alive and jumping | Frozen solid | *Cooked in hot oil or fat | Dressed up in a costume
